Formal Architecture Specifications

C.1 System-of-Systems Formalization

H-ACE is a tuple:

\text{H-ACE} = \langle \text{Human}, \text{Physical}, \text{Digital}, \text{Governance}, \text{Interfaces} \rangle

Where:

\text{Human} = \{ \text{Residents}, \text{Staff}, \text{Families}, \text{Clinicians}, \text{Educators}, \text{Community Partners} \}

\text{Physical} = \{ \text{Campus}, \text{Energy}, \text{Water}, \text{Buildings}, \text{Robotics}, \text{Environmental Systems} \}

\text{Digital} = \{ \text{Data Fabric}, \text{Digital Twin}, \text{Security AI}, \text{Rehabilitation Intelligence}, \text{Cybersecurity}, \text{Audit Logs} \}

\text{Governance} = \{ \text{Law}, \text{Ethics}, \text{Oversight}, \text{HARB}, \text{Appeals} \}

C.2 Interface Control Matrix

Source Destination Data Type Allowed Control
Security AI Human Security Team Alerts, risk notifications Yes Human review
Rehabilitation Intelligence Rehabilitation Team Recommendations Yes Human review
Security AI Rehabilitation AI Direct data exchange No Cryptographically isolated
Clinical Systems Security AI Clinical data No Emergency exception with audit
Digital Twin Physical Systems Monitoring, simulation Yes Read-only for control
Governance All Systems Audit, inspection Yes Unrestricted within legal bounds
AI Physical Restraint / Medication Control signals No Hard prohibition

C.3 State Transition Model for High-Impact Decisions

Let S be a high-impact decision state. A transition to state S' is valid if and only if:

\text{Transition}(S \rightarrow S') \implies \exists h \in \text{HumanDecisionMakers}: \text{SignOff}(h, S')

An automated recommendation may propose S', but cannot enact S' without h.

Formally:

\forall \text{AI Output}: \text{Output}_{\text{AI}} \notin \text{FinalState}

\text{FinalState} \in \text{HumanApprovalSet}

This ensures no high-impact decision is made solely by AI.

