Appendix U

Formal Proofs of Architectural Separation

U.1 Proof: AI Cannot Control Physical Restraint

Theorem: No interface shall permit direct AI control over physical restraint, medication, solitary confinement, or involuntary movement.

Proof:

1. Let C_{\text{AI}} be the set of AI system outputs.
2. Let A_{\text{phys}} be the set of physical actuators including restraint, medication administration, solitary confinement doors, involuntary movement systems.
3. By HACE-ARCH-002, no interface exists between C_{\text{AI}} and A_{\text{phys}}.
4. An AI system can only affect the physical world through interfaces that connect its outputs to actuators.
5. Therefore, no AI output can directly control A_{\text{phys}}. \square

U.2 Proof: Data Isolation Between Security AI and Rehabilitation AI

Theorem: Security AI shall not access rehabilitation data, and Rehabilitation AI shall not access security data.

Proof:

1. Let D_S be Security AI data domain, D_R be Rehabilitation AI data domain.
2. By data classification table, D_S \cap D_R = \emptyset except for controlled gateway data.
3. Network segmentation ensures no direct data flow from Security AI to Rehabilitation AI.
4. Therefore, Security AI cannot access rehabilitation data and vice versa. \square

